  "limitations": [
    "Exact-value shielded withdrawals only; partial spends, durable change settlement and spent-input recovery remain refused/deferred (#201). Compatible value-host support remains #202.",
    "No full Lace compatibility claim (#81), full typed circuit coverage (#82), real passkey-provider restoration or two-browser acceptance (#232). Synthetic credentials do not qualify providers.",
    "Entry removal excludes one roster entry from fresh keys; it cannot erase prior disclosures or certify full compromised-identity retirement (#228/#229). Total-loss recovery remains unavailable (#240).",
    "Grant bookkeeping requires the original publishing reader; surviving ACC viewing access alone does not recover another reader's bookkeeping or missing staged/grantee secrets (#239).",
    "Durable owner/host jobs are opt-in APIs, separate from the default demo and volatile legacy jobs. Missing/ambiguous originals stay unknown; no automatic scanner, distributed sponsor lock, persistent spending budget, general no-send repair or journal compaction (#230/#233/#234).",
    "Native proof/restart evidence retains its actual historical source/image revisions and interruption boundaries. No fresh native lifecycle was run on the RC6 published images. Linux state volumes are qualified; macOS bind-backed image journals are not (#231).",
    "Lifecycle grant/holding setup and wallet credit were standalone operations, not job-backed value transfers. Canonical node/indexer checks trust that pair and are not light-client proofs.",
    "NIGHT funding is qualified only on the pinned undeployed localnet, in smallest units. Other networks need dedicated funded wallets, explicit policy and separate acceptance. Proof servers receive private proof inputs; restrict ingress."
  ],
